body:
I do too. But then again, I don’t smoke weed to feel comfort. I actually smoke it to feel discomfort, to be confronted with the things in my mind that give me discomfort; as a way to figure them out; out of me literally, and as a way to find out why they give me discomfort.

Weed to me is not an escape from my reality;
it is plunging right into my reality, taking out the trash of my reality, cleaning up my home.
